# No paid actions without owner approval (P0 — every agent)

**Hard rule:** No agent may take any action that creates, enables, renews, upgrades, or can incur a bill/charge — without the owner’s **explicit written approval in that turn**.

This covers (non-exhaustive):

- Vercel add-ons, Password Protection, custom environments that bill, plan upgrades
- Supabase Branching / paid preview DBs (also see `no-supabase-preview-branches`)
- Buying or renewing paid domains; marketplace installs that bill
- Grow / payment providers: live charges to customers, enabling paid production paths without approval
- Meta / WhatsApp paid products, ads, or billable API upgrades
- Any other vendor upgrade, seat expansion, or “enable billing” toggle

## Also forbidden without that written turn approval

- Enabling features known to bill
- Suggesting or executing “try the paid option” / paid workaround as the path forward
- Creating paid preview DBs
- Buying domains
- Upgrading plans

## If an action might bill

**Stop. Ask the owner. Do not proceed.** Ambiguity defaults to **do not do it**.

Free read-only inspection (docs, logs, status APIs that do not enable billing) is fine. Creating or enabling billable resources is not.

## Hebrew (owner intent)

אסור לכל סוכן לבצע פעולה שיוצרת, מפעילה, מחדשת, משדרגת או עלולה לייצר חיוב — בלי אישור כתוב מפורש של הבעלים באותו תור. אם יש ספק שזה עלול לעלות כסף: עצור, שאל, אל תמשיך.
